cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PLECTA: overlap-aware reconstruction of filament instances from binary axis masks"
message: "If you use this software, or the method it implements, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Allan
    given-names: Oday
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6341-4695"
    affiliation: "University of Twente"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jorallan/PLECTA"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22687992"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-10"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - filament segmentation
  - instance segmentation
  - overlapping instances
  - skeleton analysis
  - microscopy image analysis
abstract: >-
  PLECTA reconstructs overlapping strand instances from a thin binary mask. It
  skeletonizes the mask, decomposes it into arms and junctions, and alternates
  exact crossing matching with gated gap matching as chain geometry is refined.
  Grouping is deterministic and mask-only: it reads neither the source image,
  the ground truth, nor a clean reference mask, and crossing pixels may belong
  to several output instances.
